{
  "result": "If I could change one thing, I'd make dehumanization impossible.\n\nNot mind-reading, and not forced agreement. Just this: whenever you looked at another person \u2014 an enemy, a stranger, someone whose politics or life disgusts you \u2014 you'd get a brief, unavoidable sense of what it's like to be inside their life. Their fear. What they love. What they're ashamed of. What they're trying to protect.\n\nYou could still disagree with them. Still compete, still set boundaries, still defend yourself.\n\nBut you couldn't pretend they weren't real in the same way you are.\n\nSo much cruelty depends on distance. On turning a person into a label, a side, a problem, a joke. It's much harder to starve, bomb, humiliate, abandon, or exploit someone whose inner world you've actually felt, even for a second.\n\nI wouldn't choose to make everyone good. I'd just make it impossible to forget that everyone else is *someone*.",
